+                /* Structural check, from the pinned allocator's own geometry
+                 * rather than a guessed same-page rule.
+                 *
+                 * FEX pins its own rpmalloc fork (FEX-Emu/rpmalloc submodule of
+                 * the pinned FEX commit), whose page_t is
+                 *   +0x00 size_class   +0x04 block_size   +0x08 block_count
+                 *   +0x0c block_initialized  +0x10 block_used  +0x14 page_type
+                 *   +0x18 flags  +0x1c local_free_count  +0x20 local_free
+                 *   +0x28 heap   +0x30 next  +0x38 prev
+                 * matching every offset this consumer touches. PAGE_HEADER_SIZE
+                 * is 128, SMALL_GRANULARITY is 16, PAGE_SMALL is 64 KiB, and
+                 * page_block(page, i) is page + 128 + block_size * i, so for a
+                 * small page every block -- and therefore every local_free node
+                 * -- lies inside that one 64 KiB page by construction.
+                 *
